IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: Part 5 Division 4 -- the register of members kept by a public company
-- (ss 189A to 196). Layer 1: the law, objectively. Part sgm. Text: the SSO informal consolidation as the file renders it (a rendering, not the official text).
--
-- WHAT THIS MODULE DOES. For each provision it states, as a function over facts a witness can state, what the text says:
-- the duties of a public company about its register of members and its index, where they are kept, closing and inspection,
-- the copy a person may ask for, the default of the agent who keeps the register, rectification by the Court, the trustee's protection,
-- branch registers, and the offences. Duties with a stated time limit are also regulative rules with a trace that reaches BREACH.
--
-- READING A RESULT. MAYBE BOOLEAN: JUST TRUE is yes; JUST FALSE is the text saying no in its own words; NOTHING is "the text does not say"
-- (NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (sgm)"). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
--
-- PERIODS. A duty to act "within N days after X" is answered with `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` (the last
-- day is X plus N; an early act is in time), because a duty has a closing edge and the text names no opening edge (fork F-P2 in NOTES.md).
-- The window function `period: the date is within a period after` would turn an act on the very day of the event into a default.

§ `Section 189A: application and interpretation of the Division`

-- src below: 189A(1).
-- src:17097 | Application and interpretation of Division
-- src:17099 | 189A.—(1) This Division applies only in relation to a public
-- src:17100 | company.
@ref s 189A(1) (src:17097-17100)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 189A(1) this Division applies to the company` MEANS
    IF `the company is a public company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Division applies only in relation to a public company." ("only" closes the scope)

-- src:17104 | (2) In this Division, a reference to the register means the register of
-- src:17105 | members required to be kept by a public company under
-- src:17106 | section 190(1).
@ref s 189A(2) (src:17104-17106)
GIVEN `the register is the register of members required to be kept by a public company under section 190(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 189A(2) the register is the register of this Division` MEANS
    IF `the register is the register of members required to be kept by a public company under section 190(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a reference to the register means the register of members required to be kept by a public company under section 190(1)" (a "means" definition)

§ `Section 190(1): the register of members and what is entered in it`

-- What the register shows, one fact per entry the subsection requires. A witness can read each off the register.
DECLARE `s 190(1) register entries` HAS
    `the register enters the names and addresses of the members` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the register enters a statement of the shares held by each member, distinguishing each share by its number (if any) or by the number (if any) of the certificate evidencing the member's holding` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the register enters the amount paid or agreed to be considered as paid on the shares of each member` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the register enters the date at which the name of each person was entered in the register as a member` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the register enters the date at which any person who ceased to be a member during the previous 7 years so ceased to be a member` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the register enters the date of every allotment of shares to members and the number of shares comprised in each allotment` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:17110 | Register and index of members of public companies
-- src:17112 | 190.—(1) Every public company must keep a register of its
-- src:17113 | members and enter therein —
@ref s 190(1) (src:17110-17113)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 190(1) the company must keep a register of its members` MEANS
    `s 189A(1) this Division applies to the company` `the company is a public company`   -- JUST TRUE for a public company; JUST FALSE for any other because s 189A(1) says the Division applies "only" to a public company

-- src:17115 | (a) the names and addresses of the members, and in the case of
-- src:17116 | a public company having a share capital a statement of the
-- src:17117 | shares held by each member, distinguishing each share by
-- src:17118 | its number (if any) or by the number (if any) of the
-- src:17119 | certificate evidencing the member’s holding and of the
-- src:17120 | amount paid or agreed to be considered as paid on the
-- src:17121 | shares of each member;
@ref s 190(1)(a) (src:17115-17121)
GIVEN entries IS A `s 190(1) register entries`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 190(1)(a) the register enters the names and addresses and, for a company having a share capital, the statement of shares` MEANS
    IF     entries's `the register enters the names and addresses of the members`
       AND (IF entries's `the company has a share capital`
            THEN entries's `the register enters a statement of the shares held by each member, distinguishing each share by its number (if any) or by the number (if any) of the certificate evidencing the member's holding`
                 AND entries's `the register enters the amount paid or agreed to be considered as paid on the shares of each member`
            ELSE TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every public company must keep a register of its members and enter therein (a) the names and addresses of the members, and in the case of a public company having a share capital a statement of the shares held by each member ..." (a duty not met: the provision's own question)

-- src:17123 | (b) the date at which the name of each person was entered in
-- src:17124 | the register as a member;
@ref s 190(1)(b) (src:17123-17124)
GIVEN entries IS A `s 190(1) register entries`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 190(1)(b) the register enters the date at which the name of each person was entered as a member` MEANS
    IF entries's `the register enters the date at which the name of each person was entered in the register as a member`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must keep a register of its members and enter therein (b) the date at which the name of each person was entered in the register as a member" (a duty not met)

-- src:17126 | (c) the date at which any person who ceased to be a member
-- src:17127 | during the previous 7 years so ceased to be a member; and
@ref s 190(1)(c) (src:17126-17127)
GIVEN entries IS A `s 190(1) register entries`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 190(1)(c) the register enters the date at which a person who ceased to be a member during the previous 7 years ceased` MEANS
    IF entries's `the register enters the date at which any person who ceased to be a member during the previous 7 years so ceased to be a member`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must keep a register of its members and enter therein (c) the date at which any person who ceased to be a member during the previous 7 years so ceased to be a member" (a duty not met)

-- src:17129 | (d) in the case of a public company having a share capital, the
-- src:17130 | date of every allotment of shares to members and the
-- src:17131 | number of shares comprised in each allotment.
@ref s 190(1)(d) (src:17129-17131)
GIVEN entries IS A `s 190(1) register entries`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 190(1)(d) the register enters the date and size of every allotment, for a company having a share capital` MEANS
    IF (NOT entries's `the company has a share capital`) OR entries's `the register enters the date of every allotment of shares to members and the number of shares comprised in each allotment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(d) in the case of a public company having a share capital, the date of every allotment of shares to members and the number of shares comprised in each allotment" (a duty not met; a company with no share capital has nothing to enter)

-- (1) as a whole: every entry the subsection requires.
-- src:17110 | Register and index of members of public companies
-- src:17112 | 190.—(1) Every public company must keep a register of its
-- src:17113 | members and enter therein —
-- src:17115 | (a) the names and addresses of the members, and in the case of
-- src:17116 | a public company having a share capital a statement of the
-- src:17117 | shares held by each member, distinguishing each share by
-- src:17118 | its number (if any) or by the number (if any) of the
-- src:17119 | certificate evidencing the member’s holding and of the
-- src:17120 | amount paid or agreed to be considered as paid on the
-- src:17121 | shares of each member;
-- src:17123 | (b) the date at which the name of each person was entered in
-- src:17124 | the register as a member;
-- src:17126 | (c) the date at which any person who ceased to be a member
-- src:17127 | during the previous 7 years so ceased to be a member; and
-- src:17129 | (d) in the case of a public company having a share capital, the
-- src:17130 | date of every allotment of shares to members and the
-- src:17131 | number of shares comprised in each allotment.
@ref s 190(1) (src:17110-17131)
GIVEN entries IS A `s 190(1) register entries`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 190(1) the register has every entry the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF     `s 190(1)(a) the register enters the names and addresses and, for a company having a share capital, the statement of shares` entries EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND `s 190(1)(b) the register enters the date at which the name of each person was entered as a member` entries EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND `s 190(1)(c) the register enters the date at which a person who ceased to be a member during the previous 7 years ceased` entries EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND `s 190(1)(d) the register enters the date and size of every allotment, for a company having a share capital` entries EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every public company must keep a register of its members and enter therein (a) ...; (b) ...; (c) ...; and (d) ..." (a duty not met: the provision's own question)

-- The keel asks (s 4(1) "principal register"): is this register the register of members kept pursuant to section 190?
-- src:17110 | Register and index of members of public companies
-- src:17112 | 190.—(1) Every public company must keep a register of its
-- src:17113 | members and enter therein —
@ref s 190(1) (src:17110-17113)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the register is the register of members of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 190(1) the register is the register of members of the company kept pursuant to section 190` MEANS
    IF `the company is a public company`
    THEN (IF `the register is the register of members of the company` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section names no other register of a public company
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): s 189A(1) "This Division applies only in relation to a public company" (s 190 is in the Division; the old register s 196D keeps for 7 years is the register "in force immediately before 3 January 2016", not one kept pursuant to this section as it now reads)

§ `Section 190(2): shares converted into stock`

-- src:17135 | (2) Despite anything in subsection (1), where the public company
-- src:17136 | has converted any of its shares into stock and given notice of the
-- src:17137 | conversion to the Registrar, the company must alter the register to
-- src:17138 | show the amount of stock or number of stock units held by each
-- src:17143 | member instead of the number of shares and the particulars relating to
-- src:17144 | shares specified in subsection (1)(a).
@ref s 190(2) (src:17135-17144)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the public company has converted any of its shares into stock` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the public company has given notice of the conversion to the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 190(2) the company must alter the register to show stock instead of shares` MEANS
    IF `the company is a public company` AND `the public company has converted any of its shares into stock` AND `the public company has given notice of the conversion to the Registrar`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the public company has converted any of its shares into stock and given notice of the conversion to the Registrar, the company must alter the register" (a duty gated by "where": ruling (b) of the periods ruling, fork F-W1)

-- src:17135 | (2) Despite anything in subsection (1), where the public company
-- src:17136 | has converted any of its shares into stock and given notice of the
-- src:17137 | conversion to the Registrar, the company must alter the register to
-- src:17138 | show the amount of stock or number of stock units held by each
-- src:17143 | member instead of the number of shares and the particulars relating to
-- src:17144 | shares specified in subsection (1)(a).
@ref s 190(2) (src:17135-17144)
GIVEN `the register shows the amount of stock or number of stock units held by each member instead of the number of shares and the particulars relating to shares specified in subsection (1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 190(2) the register has been altered as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the register shows the amount of stock or number of stock units held by each member instead of the number of shares and the particulars relating to shares specified in subsection (1)(a)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company must alter the register to show the amount of stock or number of stock units held by each member instead of the number of shares" (a duty not met: the provision's own question; call it only where `s 190(2) the company must alter the register to show stock instead of shares` is JUST TRUE)

§ `Section 190(2A): shares or stocks a public company buys under section 76H`

-- src:17148 | (2A) Where a public company purchases one or more of its own
-- src:17149 | shares or stocks in circumstances in which section 76H applies —
-- src:17151 | (a) the requirements of subsections (1)(a), (b) and (c) and (2)
-- src:17152 | must be complied with unless the public company cancels
-- src:17153 | all of the shares or stocks immediately after the purchase in
-- src:17154 | accordance with section 76K(1); but
@ref s 190(2A)(a) (src:17148-17154)
GIVEN `the public company purchases one or more of its own shares or stocks in circumstances in which section 76H applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the public company cancels all of the shares or stocks immediately after the purchase in accordance with section 76K(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 190(2A)(a) the requirements of subsections (1)(a), (b) and (c) and (2) must be complied with` MEANS
    IF `the public company purchases one or more of its own shares or stocks in circumstances in which section 76H applies`
    THEN (IF `the public company cancels all of the shares or stocks immediately after the purchase in accordance with section 76K(1)`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be complied with unless the public company cancels all of the shares or stocks immediately after the purchase" ("unless" met)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a public company purchases one or more of its own shares or stocks in circumstances in which section 76H applies" (the "Where" gate unmet: ruling (b) of the periods ruling, fork F-W1)

-- src:17156 | (b) any share or stock which is so cancelled is to be
-- src:17157 | disregarded for the purposes of subsections (1)(a) and (2).
@ref s 190(2A)(b) (src:17156-17157)
GIVEN `the public company purchases one or more of its own shares or stocks in circumstances in which section 76H applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the share or stock is so cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 190(2A)(b) the share or stock is disregarded for the purposes of subsections (1)(a) and (2)` MEANS
    IF `the public company purchases one or more of its own shares or stocks in circumstances in which section 76H applies` AND `the share or stock is so cancelled`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any share or stock which is so cancelled is to be disregarded" names the cancelled share or stock only, and says nothing of any other (fork F-W2)

