GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 190(3) the company need not supply the names and particulars of former members` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person applies for a copy of the register`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the provision speaks of "any person who applies for a copy of the register" and says nothing of anyone else
    ELSE (IF `the person specifically requests the names and particulars of former members`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "need not be supplied ... unless the person specifically requests the names and particulars of former members" ("unless" met; fork F-U1)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

