    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "prima facie evidence of any matters inserted therein as required or authorised by this Act" -- the text speaks of those matters and is silent on any other

§ `Section 190(5) and (6): the index of members`

-- src:17173 | Index of members of public company
-- src:17175 | (5) Every public company having more than 50 members must,
-- src:17176 | unless the register of members is in such a form as to constitute in
-- src:17177 | itself an index, keep an index in convenient form of the names of the
-- src:17178 | members and must, within 14 days after the date on which any
-- src:17179 | alteration is made in the register of members, make any necessary
-- src:17180 | alteration in the index.
@ref s 190(5) (src:17173-17180)
GIVEN `the number of members of the company` IS A NUMBER
      `the register of members is in such a form as to constitute in itself an index` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 190(5) the public company must keep an index of the names of its members` MEANS
    IF `the number of members of the company` AT MOST 50
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every public company having more than 50 members must" is a scope limit with no "only"; the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c) (fork F-S1)
    ELSE (IF `the register of members is in such a form as to constitute in itself an index`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, unless the register of members is in such a form as to constitute in itself an index, keep an index"
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

