@ref s 190(6) (src:17184-17186)
GIVEN `the index contains, in respect of each member, a sufficient indication to enable the account of that member in the register to be readily found` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 190(6) the index has the indication the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the index contains, in respect of each member, a sufficient indication to enable the account of that member in the register to be readily found`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The index must in respect of each member contain a sufficient indication to enable the account of that member in the register to be readily found" (a duty not met; the text names no bearer, so there is no regulative rule: fork F-B1)

§ `Section 190(7): the offence`

-- src:17188 | (7) If default is made in complying with this section, the public
-- src:17189 | company and every officer of the company who is in default shall be
-- src:17194 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:17195 | exceeding $1,000 and also to a default penalty.
@ref s 190(7) (src:17188-17195)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 190` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 190(7) the public company is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with section 190`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (split site (i), fork F-O1): "If default is made in complying with this section, the public company and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence" -- the "If" is unmet, so this subsection makes the company guilty of nothing on these facts (the status-quo reading (a))

-- src:17188 | (7) If default is made in complying with this section, the public
-- src:17189 | company and every officer of the company who is in default shall be
-- src:17194 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:17195 | exceeding $1,000 and also to a default penalty.
@ref s 190(7) (src:17188-17195)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 190` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer of the company is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 190(7) the officer of the company is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with section 190` AND `the officer of the company is in default`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (split site (i), fork F-O1): "the public company and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet (no default made, or this officer is not in default)

-- src:17188 | (7) If default is made in complying with this section, the public
-- src:17189 | company and every officer of the company who is in default shall be
-- src:17194 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:17195 | exceeding $1,000 and also to a default penalty.
@ref s 190(7) (src:17188-17195)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 190` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer of the company is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Penalty`
`s 190(7) the most the officer of the company may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 190(7) the officer of the company is guilty of an offence` `default is made in complying with section 190` `the officer of the company is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`Penalty` OF 1000, 0, FALSE, TRUE)   -- a fine not exceeding $1,000 and also a default penalty; no imprisonment
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for those it makes guilty

-- src:17188 | (7) If default is made in complying with this section, the public
-- src:17189 | company and every officer of the company who is in default shall be
-- src:17194 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:17195 | exceeding $1,000 and also to a default penalty.
@ref s 190(7) (src:17188-17195)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 190` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Penalty`
`s 190(7) the most the public company may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 190(7) the public company is guilty of an offence` `default is made in complying with section 190` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`Penalty` OF 1000, 0, FALSE, TRUE)   -- a fine not exceeding $1,000 and also a default penalty; no imprisonment
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for those it makes guilty

§ `Regulative rules of section 190: keep the register, keep the index, alter the index in time`

DECLARE `s 190 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 190(1) keep a register of its members and enter in it what the subsection requires`
    `s 190(5) keep an index in convenient form of the names of the members`
    `s 190(5) alter the index to show the alteration made in the register of members`

-- (1): the duty has no time limit in the text, and its consequence (the offence of s 190(7)) attaches to "default", not to a time:
-- no trace can show it breached (listed in NOTES.md, "Rules with no breach path (sgm)").
-- src:17110 | Register and index of members of public companies
-- src:17112 | 190.—(1) Every public company must keep a register of its
-- src:17113 | members and enter therein —
@ref s 190(1) (src:17110-17113)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 190 act`
`s 190(1) a public company must keep a register of its members` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 190(1) keep a register of its members and enter in it what the subsection requires`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 190(1) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the public company did not keep a register of its members with the entries the subsection requires" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: maintenance; see notes]

-- (5), first duty: keep the index. No time limit: no breach path.
-- src:17175 | (5) Every public company having more than 50 members must,
-- src:17176 | unless the register of members is in such a form as to constitute in
-- src:17177 | itself an index, keep an index in convenient form of the names of the
-- src:17178 | members and must, within 14 days after the date on which any
@ref s 190(5) (src:17175-17178)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 190 act`
`s 190(5) a public company having more than 50 members must keep an index of the names of the members` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 190(5) keep an index in convenient form of the names of the members`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 190(5) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the public company did not keep an index of the names of its members" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: maintenance; see notes]

-- (5), second duty: "within 14 days after the date on which any alteration is made in the register of members, make any necessary alteration in the index".
-- The trace clock counts days from the day of the alteration of the register (AT 0).
-- src:17178 | members and must, within 14 days after the date on which any
-- src:17179 | alteration is made in the register of members, make any necessary
-- src:17180 | alteration in the index.
@ref s 190(5) (src:17178-17180)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 190 act`
`s 190(5) a public company must alter the index within 14 days after an alteration of the register` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 190(5) alter the index to show the alteration made in the register of members`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the public company did not alter the index within 14 days after the alteration made in the register of members"

§ `Section 191: where the register is kept`

-- Where the register and index are kept. The constructors name the places (a) and (b) allow and the places they do not.
DECLARE `s 191(1) place where the register and index are kept` IS ONE OF
    `s 191(1) the registered office of the public company`
    `s 191(1)(a) another office of the company in Singapore at which the work of making them up is done`
    `s 191(1)(a) another office of the company in Singapore at which that work is not done`
    `s 191(1)(b) the office in Singapore of the other person with whom the company has arranged to make them up, at which that work is done`
    `s 191(1)(b) an office in Singapore of that other person at which that work is not done`
    `s 191(1)(b) an office of that other person outside Singapore`
    `s 191(1) some other place`

-- src:17204 | (a) if the work of making them up is done at another office of
-- src:17205 | the company in Singapore they may be kept at that other
-- src:17206 | office; or
@ref s 191(1)(a) (src:17204-17206)
GIVEN `the work of making up the register and index is done at another office of the company in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 191(1)(a) the register and index may be kept at that other office` MEANS
    IF `the work of making up the register and index is done at another office of the company in Singapore`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) if the work of making them up is done at another office of the company in Singapore they may be kept at that other office" (a grant whose "if" gate failed; the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork F-G1)

-- src:17208 | (b) if the company arranges with some other person to make
-- src:17209 | up the register and index (if any) on its behalf they may be
-- src:17210 | kept at the office of that other person at which the work is
-- src:17211 | done if that office is in Singapore.
@ref s 191(1)(b) (src:17208-17211)
GIVEN `the company arranges with some other person to make up the register and index on its behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the office is the office of that other person at which the work is done` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that office is in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 191(1)(b) the register and index may be kept at the office of that other person` MEANS
    IF `the company arranges with some other person to make up the register and index on its behalf` AND `the office is the office of that other person at which the work is done` AND `that office is in Singapore`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) if the company arranges with some other person to make up the register and index (if any) on its behalf they may be kept at the office of that other person at which the work is done if that office is in Singapore" (a grant whose "if" gates failed; the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork F-G1)

-- src:17201 | 191.—(1) The register of members and index (if any) must be kept
-- src:17202 | at the registered office of the public company, but —
-- src:17204 | (a) if the work of making them up is done at another office of
-- src:17205 | the company in Singapore they may be kept at that other
-- src:17206 | office; or
-- src:17208 | (b) if the company arranges with some other person to make
-- src:17209 | up the register and index (if any) on its behalf they may be
-- src:17210 | kept at the office of that other person at which the work is
-- src:17211 | done if that office is in Singapore.
@ref s 191(1) (src:17201-17211)
GIVEN place IS A `s 191(1) place where the register and index are kept`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 191(1) the place where the register and index are kept is one the subsection allows` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `s 191(1) the registered office of the public company` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 191(1)(a) another office of the company in Singapore at which the work of making them up is done` THEN `s 191(1)(a) the register and index may be kept at that other office` TRUE
    WHEN `s 191(1)(b) the office in Singapore of the other person with whom the company has arranged to make them up, at which that work is done` THEN `s 191(1)(b) the register and index may be kept at the office of that other person` TRUE TRUE TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The register of members and index (if any) must be kept at the registered office of the public company, but" only (a) and (b) allow another place (a duty not met: the provision's own question)

DECLARE `s 191(2) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 191(2) lodge with the Registrar notice of the place where the register and index are kept, or of the change`

-- src:17215 | (2) Every public company must, within 14 days after the register
-- src:17216 | and index, if any, are first kept at a place other than the registered
-- src:17217 | office, lodge with the Registrar notice of the place where the register
-- src:17218 | and index (if any) are kept and must, within 14 days after any change
-- src:17219 | in the place at which the register and index (if any) are kept, lodge
-- src:17220 | with the Registrar notice of the change.
@ref s 191(2) (src:17215-17220)
GIVEN `the register and index are first kept at a place other than the registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a change in the place at which the register and index are kept` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 191(2) the public company must lodge notice with the Registrar` MEANS
    IF `the register and index are first kept at a place other than the registered office` OR `there is a change in the place at which the register and index are kept`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the duty arises "after the register and index ... are first kept at a place other than the registered office" and "after any change in the place"; on no such event the text says nothing (fork F-E1)

-- src:17215 | (2) Every public company must, within 14 days after the register
-- src:17216 | and index, if any, are first kept at a place other than the registered
-- src:17217 | office, lodge with the Registrar notice of the place where the register
-- src:17218 | and index (if any) are kept and must, within 14 days after any change
-- src:17219 | in the place at which the register and index (if any) are kept, lodge
-- src:17220 | with the Registrar notice of the change.
@ref s 191(2) (src:17215-17220)
GIVEN `the day on which the register and index are first kept at a place other than the registered office, or on which the place changes` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 191(2) the last day for lodging the notice` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the day on which the register and index are first kept at a place other than the registered office, or on which the place changes` 14 Days

-- src:17215 | (2) Every public company must, within 14 days after the register
-- src:17216 | and index, if any, are first kept at a place other than the registered
-- src:17217 | office, lodge with the Registrar notice of the place where the register
-- src:17218 | and index (if any) are kept and must, within 14 days after any change
-- src:17219 | in the place at which the register and index (if any) are kept, lodge
-- src:17220 | with the Registrar notice of the change.
@ref s 191(2) (src:17215-17220)
GIVEN `the day on which the register and index are first kept at a place other than the registered office, or on which the place changes` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the notice is lodged with the Registrar` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 191(2) the notice was lodged within 14 days` MEANS
    `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day on which the register and index are first kept at a place other than the registered office, or on which the place changes` `the day on which the notice is lodged with the Registrar` 14 Days

-- src:17215 | (2) Every public company must, within 14 days after the register
-- src:17216 | and index, if any, are first kept at a place other than the registered
-- src:17217 | office, lodge with the Registrar notice of the place where the register
-- src:17218 | and index (if any) are kept and must, within 14 days after any change
-- src:17219 | in the place at which the register and index (if any) are kept, lodge
-- src:17220 | with the Registrar notice of the change.
@ref s 191(2) (src:17215-17220)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 191(2) act`
`s 191(2) a public company must lodge notice with the Registrar within 14 days` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 191(2) lodge with the Registrar notice of the place where the register and index are kept, or of the change`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the public company did not lodge notice of the place where the register and index are kept, or of the change, within 14 days"

-- src:17224 | (3) If default is made in complying with this section, the public
-- src:17225 | company and every officer of the company who is in default shall be
-- src:17226 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:17227 | exceeding $1,000 and also to a default penalty.
@ref s 191(3) (src:17224-17227)
