GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 191(3) the public company is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with section 191`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (split site (i), fork F-O1): "If default is made in complying with this section, the public company and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence" -- the "If" is unmet

-- src:17224 | (3) If default is made in complying with this section, the public
-- src:17225 | company and every officer of the company who is in default shall be
-- src:17226 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:17227 | exceeding $1,000 and also to a default penalty.
@ref s 191(3) (src:17224-17227)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 191` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer of the company is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 191(3) the officer of the company is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with section 191` AND `the officer of the company is in default`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (split site (i), fork F-O1): "the public company and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet

-- src:17224 | (3) If default is made in complying with this section, the public
-- src:17225 | company and every officer of the company who is in default shall be
-- src:17226 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:17227 | exceeding $1,000 and also to a default penalty.
@ref s 191(3) (src:17224-17227)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 191` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Penalty`
`s 191(3) the most the public company or an officer in default may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 191(3) the public company is guilty of an offence` `default is made in complying with section 191` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`Penalty` OF 1000, 0, FALSE, TRUE)   -- a fine not exceeding $1,000 and also a default penalty; no imprisonment
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for those it makes guilty

§ `Section 192: closing, inspection and copies of the register`

-- src:17233 | 192.—(1) A public company may close the register of members or
-- src:17234 | any class of members for one or more periods not exceeding 30 days
@ref s 192(1) (src:17233-17234)
GIVEN `the total number of days in the calendar year for which the register of members or any class of members is closed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 192(1) the public company may close the register of members or a class of members for the periods` MEANS
    IF `the total number of days in the calendar year for which the register of members or any class of members is closed` AT MOST 30
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A public company may close the register ... for one or more periods not exceeding 30 days in the aggregate in any calendar year" (a grant limited by its own wording; the case falls outside the limit; fork F-G2)

-- src:17239 | (2) The register and index must be open to the inspection of any
-- src:17240 | member without charge and of any other person on payment for each
-- src:17241 | inspection of $1 or such less sum as the public company requires.
@ref s 192(2) (src:17239-17241)
GIVEN `the person inspecting is a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person inspecting pays for the inspection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 192(2) the register and index must be open to the person's inspection` MEANS
    IF `the person inspecting is a member of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE (IF `the person inspecting pays for the inspection`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "and of any other person on payment for each inspection of $1 or such less sum as the public company requires" (the duty to open the register to a non-member is tied to payment; the text is silent when none is made)

-- src:17239 | (2) The register and index must be open to the inspection of any
-- src:17240 | member without charge and of any other person on payment for each
-- src:17241 | inspection of $1 or such less sum as the public company requires.
@ref s 192(2) (src:17239-17241)
GIVEN `the person inspecting is a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the charge the company requires for one inspection, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 192(2) the charge the company requires for an inspection is one the subsection allows` MEANS
    IF `the person inspecting is a member of the company`
    THEN (IF `the charge the company requires for one inspection, in dollars` EQUALS 0 THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "open to the inspection of any member without charge"
    ELSE (IF `the charge the company requires for one inspection, in dollars` AT MOST 1 THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any other person on payment for each inspection of $1 or such less sum as the public company requires" (the price of an inspection is $1 or less; fork F-C1)

DECLARE `s 192(2) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 192(2) open the register and index to inspection`

-- src:17239 | (2) The register and index must be open to the inspection of any
