-- src:17261 | (4) If any copy so requested is not sent within the period prescribed
-- src:17262 | by subsection (3), the public company and every officer of the
-- src:17263 | company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence and shall be
-- src:17264 | liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $400 and also to a default
-- src:17265 | penalty.
@ref s 192(4) (src:17261-17265)
GIVEN `any copy so requested is not sent within the period prescribed by subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 192(4) the public company is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `any copy so requested is not sent within the period prescribed by subsection (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (split site (i), fork F-O1): "If any copy so requested is not sent within the period prescribed by subsection (3), the public company and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence" -- the "If" is unmet

-- src:17261 | (4) If any copy so requested is not sent within the period prescribed
-- src:17262 | by subsection (3), the public company and every officer of the
-- src:17263 | company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence and shall be
-- src:17264 | liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $400 and also to a default
-- src:17265 | penalty.
@ref s 192(4) (src:17261-17265)
GIVEN `any copy so requested is not sent within the period prescribed by subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer of the company is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 192(4) the officer of the company is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `any copy so requested is not sent within the period prescribed by subsection (3)` AND `the officer of the company is in default`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (split site (i), fork F-O1): "the public company and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet

-- src:17261 | (4) If any copy so requested is not sent within the period prescribed
-- src:17262 | by subsection (3), the public company and every officer of the
-- src:17263 | company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence and shall be
-- src:17264 | liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $400 and also to a default
-- src:17265 | penalty.
@ref s 192(4) (src:17261-17265)
GIVEN `any copy so requested is not sent within the period prescribed by subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Penalty`
`s 192(4) the most the public company or an officer in default may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 192(4) the public company is guilty of an offence` `any copy so requested is not sent within the period prescribed by subsection (3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`Penalty` OF 400, 0, FALSE, TRUE)   -- a fine not exceeding $400 and also a default penalty; no imprisonment
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for those it makes guilty

§ `Section 193: the default of the person who keeps the register for the company`

-- src:17271 | 193. Where, by virtue of section 191(1)(b), the register of members
-- src:17272 | is kept at the office of some person other than the public company,
-- src:17273 | and by reason of any default of the person the company fails to
-- src:17274 | comply with section 191(1) or (2) or with section 192 or with any
-- src:17275 | requirements of this Act as to the production of the register, that other
-- src:17276 | person shall be liable to the same penalties as if that other person were
-- src:17277 | an officer of the company who was in default, and the power of the
-- src:17278 | Court under section 399 extends to the making of orders against that
-- src:17279 | other person and that other person’s officers and employees.
@ref s 193 (src:17271-17279)
GIVEN `the register of members is kept at the office of some person other than the public company by virtue of section 191(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company fails to comply with section 191(1) or (2), with section 192 or with any requirements of this Act as to the production of the register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure is by reason of any default of that other person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 193 the other person is liable to the same penalties as an officer of the company in default` MEANS
    IF `the register of members is kept at the office of some person other than the public company by virtue of section 191(1)(b)` AND `the company fails to comply with section 191(1) or (2), with section 192 or with any requirements of this Act as to the production of the register` AND `the failure is by reason of any default of that other person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, by virtue of section 191(1)(b), the register of members is kept at the office of some person other than the public company, and by reason of any default of the person the company fails to comply ..., that other person shall be liable to the same penalties as if that other person were an officer of the company who was in default" (a "Where" gate unmet: ruling (b) of the periods ruling; fork F-W1)

-- src:17271 | 193. Where, by virtue of section 191(1)(b), the register of members
-- src:17272 | is kept at the office of some person other than the public company,
-- src:17273 | and by reason of any default of the person the company fails to
-- src:17274 | comply with section 191(1) or (2) or with section 192 or with any
-- src:17275 | requirements of this Act as to the production of the register, that other
-- src:17276 | person shall be liable to the same penalties as if that other person were
-- src:17277 | an officer of the company who was in default, and the power of the
-- src:17278 | Court under section 399 extends to the making of orders against that
-- src:17279 | other person and that other person’s officers and employees.
@ref s 193 (src:17271-17279)
GIVEN `the register of members is kept at the office of some person other than the public company by virtue of section 191(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company fails to comply with section 191(1) or (2), with section 192 or with any requirements of this Act as to the production of the register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure is by reason of any default of that other person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 193 the power of the Court under section 399 extends to orders against that other person and that person's officers and employees` MEANS
    IF `the register of members is kept at the office of some person other than the public company by virtue of section 191(1)(b)` AND `the company fails to comply with section 191(1) or (2), with section 192 or with any requirements of this Act as to the production of the register` AND `the failure is by reason of any default of that other person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (split site (ii), fork F-G6): "Where, by virtue of section 191(1)(b), the register of members is kept at the office of some person other than the public company, and by reason of any default of the person the company fails to comply ..., the power of the Court under section 399 extends to the making of orders against that other person" -- a "Where" gate of a power (periods ruling (b); the grant ruling's limit 3 lists the site and does not change it)

DECLARE `s 193 offence the default falls under` IS ONE OF
    `s 193 the offence of section 191(3)`
    `s 193 the offence of section 192(4)`
    `s 193 an offence for failing to comply with a requirement of this Act as to the production of the register`

-- src:17271 | 193. Where, by virtue of section 191(1)(b), the register of members
-- src:17272 | is kept at the office of some person other than the public company,
-- src:17273 | and by reason of any default of the person the company fails to
-- src:17274 | comply with section 191(1) or (2) or with section 192 or with any
-- src:17275 | requirements of this Act as to the production of the register, that other
-- src:17276 | person shall be liable to the same penalties as if that other person were
-- src:17277 | an officer of the company who was in default, and the power of the
-- src:17278 | Court under section 399 extends to the making of orders against that
-- src:17279 | other person and that other person’s officers and employees.
@ref s 193 (src:17271-17279)
GIVEN offence IS A `s 193 offence the default falls under`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Penalty`
`s 193 the most the other person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    CONSIDER offence
    WHEN `s 193 the offence of section 191(3)` THEN JUST (`Penalty` OF 1000, 0, FALSE, TRUE)   -- "the same penalties as if that other person were an officer of the company who was in default": s 191(3)
    WHEN `s 193 the offence of section 192(4)` THEN JUST (`Penalty` OF 400, 0, FALSE, TRUE)   -- s 192(4)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the penalty for a requirement "as to the production of the register" is in a provision outside this range

§ `Section 194: rectification of the register by the Court`

-- Limb (a): a person's name entered in or omitted from the register without sufficient cause. Plain BOOLEAN: a condition over two facts, not the provision's answer.
-- src:17285 | 194.—(1) If —
-- src:17287 | (a) the name of any person is without sufficient cause entered
-- src:17288 | in or omitted from the register; or
@ref s 194(1)(a) (src:17285-17288)
GIVEN `the name of a person is without sufficient cause entered in the register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name of a person is without sufficient cause omitted from the register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 194(1)(a) the name of a person is without sufficient cause entered in or omitted from the register` MEANS
    `the name of a person is without sufficient cause entered in the register` OR `the name of a person is without sufficient cause omitted from the register`

-- src:17285 | 194.—(1) If —
-- src:17290 | (b) default is made or unnecessary delay takes place in
-- src:17291 | entering in the register the fact of any person having
-- src:17292 | ceased to be a member,
@ref s 194(1)(b) (src:17285-17292)
GIVEN `default is made in entering in the register the fact of a person having ceased to be a member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `unnecessary delay takes place in entering in the register the fact of a person having ceased to be a member` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 194(1)(b) default is made or unnecessary delay takes place in entering the fact of a person having ceased to be a member` MEANS
    `default is made in entering in the register the fact of a person having ceased to be a member` OR `unnecessary delay takes place in entering in the register the fact of a person having ceased to be a member`

-- src:17285 | 194.—(1) If —
-- src:17287 | (a) the name of any person is without sufficient cause entered
-- src:17288 | in or omitted from the register; or
-- src:17290 | (b) default is made or unnecessary delay takes place in
-- src:17291 | entering in the register the fact of any person having
-- src:17292 | ceased to be a member,
-- src:17297 | the person aggrieved or any member or the public company may
-- src:17298 | apply to the Court for rectification of the register, and the Court may
-- src:17299 | refuse the application or may order rectification of the register and
-- src:17300 | payment by the company of any damages sustained by any party to
-- src:17301 | the application.
@ref s 194(1) (src:17285-17301)
GIVEN `a ground in section 194(1)(a) or (b) is made out` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is the person aggrieved, a member or the public company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 194(1) the person may apply to the Court for rectification of the register` MEANS
    IF `a ground in section 194(1)(a) or (b) is made out` AND `the applicant is the person aggrieved, a member or the public company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If (a) ...; or (b) ..., the person aggrieved or any member or the public company may apply to the Court" (a grant whose "If" gate or whose list of applicants is not met; the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork F-G1)

-- src:17297 | the person aggrieved or any member or the public company may
-- src:17298 | apply to the Court for rectification of the register, and the Court may
-- src:17299 | refuse the application or may order rectification of the register and
-- src:17300 | payment by the company of any damages sustained by any party to
-- src:17301 | the application.
@ref s 194(1) (src:17297-17301)
GIVEN `an application for rectification of the register has been made under section 194(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a party to the application has sustained damages` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 194(1) the Court may order the public company to pay damages sustained by a party to the application` MEANS
    IF `an application for rectification of the register has been made under section 194(1)` AND `a party to the application has sustained damages`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Court may refuse the application or may order rectification of the register and payment by the company of any damages sustained by any party to the application" (a power of the Court on an application; silent without one)

DECLARE `s 194(2) question` IS ONE OF
    `s 194(2)(a) a question relating to the title of a party to the application to have the party's name entered in or omitted from the register`
    `s 194(2)(b) a question necessary or expedient to be decided for the rectification of the register`
    `s 194(2) some other question`

-- src:17305 | (2) On any application under subsection (1), the Court may
-- src:17306 | decide —
-- src:17308 | (a) any question relating to the title of any person who is a
-- src:17309 | party to the application to have the person’s name entered
-- src:17310 | in or omitted from the register, whether the question arises
-- src:17311 | between members or alleged members or between
-- src:17312 | members or alleged members on the one hand and the
-- src:17313 | public company on the other hand; and
-- src:17315 | (b) generally, any question necessary or expedient to be
-- src:17316 | decided for the rectification of the register.
@ref s 194(2) (src:17305-17316)
GIVEN `an application for rectification of the register has been made under section 194(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      question IS A `s 194(2) question`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 194(2) the Court may decide the question on the application` MEANS
    IF `an application for rectification of the register has been made under section 194(1)`
    THEN (CONSIDER question
          WHEN `s 194(2)(a) a question relating to the title of a party to the application to have the party's name entered in or omitted from the register` THEN JUST TRUE
          WHEN `s 194(2)(b) a question necessary or expedient to be decided for the rectification of the register` THEN JUST TRUE
          OTHERWISE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "the Court may decide (a) ...; and (b) generally, any question necessary or expedient" lists two kinds of question and does not close the list with "only"
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (split site (ii), fork F-G6): "On any application under subsection (1), the Court may decide" -- an "On" (upon) gate of a power: "upon" counts as "where" (delegated-definitions ruling (c); periods ruling (b)); the grant ruling's limit 3 lists the site and does not change it

-- (3): "so lodged" has no antecedent in this rendering of the text (finding 1 in NOTES.md); the duty is encoded as the Court's direction that a notice be lodged.
-- src:17320 | (3) The Court when making an order for rectification of the register
-- src:17321 | must by its order direct a notice of the rectification to be so lodged.
@ref s 194(3) (src:17320-17321)
GIVEN `the Court is making an order for rectification of the register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 194(3) the Court's order must direct a notice of the rectification to be lodged` MEANS
    IF `the Court is making an order for rectification of the register`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Court when making an order for rectification of the register must by its order direct a notice of the rectification to be so lodged" (a duty gated by "when"; the periods ruling item (c) counts "when" as "where"; fork F-W1)

-- (4): more than 30 years before the date of the application: the application day is later than the 30th anniversary of the entry (P4 clamps a 29 February).
-- src:17323 | (4) No application for the rectification of a register in respect of an
-- src:17324 | entry which was made in the register more than 30 years before the
-- src:17325 | date of the application may be entertained by the Court.
@ref s 194(4) (src:17323-17325)
GIVEN `the day on which the entry was made in the register` IS A DATE
      `the day of the application for rectification` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 194(4) the Court is barred from entertaining the application` MEANS
    IF `the day of the application for rectification` GREATER THAN `period: the last day of a period after` `the day on which the entry was made in the register` 30 Years
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No application ... in respect of an entry which was made in the register more than 30 years before the date of the application may be entertained" (a bar limited by its own wording; the entry is not more than 30 years old; fork F-B2)

§ `Section 195: the trustee, executor or administrator registered as holder`

-- src:17330 | 195.—(1) Any trustee, executor or administrator of the estate of
-- src:17331 | any deceased person who was registered in a register as the holder of
-- src:17332 | a share in any company may become registered as the holder of that
-- src:17333 | share as trustee, executor or administrator of that estate and is in
-- src:17334 | respect of that share subject to the same liabilities and no more as he
-- src:17335 | or she would have been subject to if the share had remained registered
-- src:17336 | in the name of the deceased person.
@ref s 195(1) (src:17330-17336)
GIVEN `the person is a trustee, executor or administrator of the estate of a deceased person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deceased person was registered in a register as the holder of a share in a company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 195(1) the trustee, executor or administrator may become registered as the holder of the share` MEANS
    IF `the person is a trustee, executor or administrator of the estate of a deceased person` AND `the deceased person was registered in a register as the holder of a share in a company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any trustee, executor or administrator of the estate of any deceased person who was registered in a register as the holder of a share in any company may become registered" (a grant limited to that person; the grant ruling, limit 1)

-- src:17330 | 195.—(1) Any trustee, executor or administrator of the estate of
-- src:17331 | any deceased person who was registered in a register as the holder of
-- src:17332 | a share in any company may become registered as the holder of that
-- src:17333 | share as trustee, executor or administrator of that estate and is in
-- src:17334 | respect of that share subject to the same liabilities and no more as he
-- src:17335 | or she would have been subject to if the share had remained registered
-- src:17336 | in the name of the deceased person.
@ref s 195(1) (src:17330-17336)
GIVEN `the person has become registered as the holder of the share as trustee, executor or administrator under section 195(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 195(1) the person is subject in respect of the share to the same liabilities and no more than the deceased person would have been` MEANS
    IF `the person has become registered as the holder of the share as trustee, executor or administrator under section 195(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the limit on liability is stated for the person who "may become registered ... and is in respect of that share subject to the same liabilities and no more"

-- src:17340 | (2) Any trustee, executor or administrator of the estate of any
-- src:17341 | deceased person who was beneficially entitled to a share in any
-- src:17342 | company being a share registered in a register may with the consent
-- src:17347 | of the company and of the registered holder of that share become
-- src:17348 | registered as the holder of the share as trustee, executor or
-- src:17349 | administrator of that estate and is in respect of the share subject to
-- src:17350 | the same liabilities and no more as he or she would have been subject
-- src:17351 | to if the share had been registered in the name of the deceased person.
@ref s 195(2) (src:17340-17351)
GIVEN `the person is a trustee, executor or administrator of the estate of a deceased person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deceased person was beneficially entitled to a share in a company, being a share registered in a register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company consents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the registered holder of the share consents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 195(2) the trustee, executor or administrator may become registered as the holder of the share` MEANS
    IF `the person is a trustee, executor or administrator of the estate of a deceased person` AND `the deceased person was beneficially entitled to a share in a company, being a share registered in a register` AND `the company consents` AND `the registered holder of the share consents`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may with the consent of the company and of the registered holder of that share become registered" (split site (ii): a "may" gated by "with the consent of"; the grant rule, `NOTHING` where the text "limits a grant or prohibition in its own wording and the case falls outside the limit"; fork F-G3)

-- src:17340 | (2) Any trustee, executor or administrator of the estate of any
-- src:17341 | deceased person who was beneficially entitled to a share in any
-- src:17342 | company being a share registered in a register may with the consent
-- src:17347 | of the company and of the registered holder of that share become
-- src:17348 | registered as the holder of the share as trustee, executor or
-- src:17349 | administrator of that estate and is in respect of the share subject to
-- src:17350 | the same liabilities and no more as he or she would have been subject
-- src:17351 | to if the share had been registered in the name of the deceased person.
@ref s 195(2) (src:17340-17351)
GIVEN `the person has become registered as the holder of the share as trustee, executor or administrator under section 195(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 195(2) the person is subject in respect of the share to the same liabilities and no more than the deceased person would have been` MEANS
    IF `the person has become registered as the holder of the share as trustee, executor or administrator under section 195(2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the limit on liability is stated for the person who "may ... become registered ... and is in respect of the share subject to the same liabilities and no more"

-- src:17355 | (3) Shares in a company registered in a register and held by a trustee
-- src:17356 | in respect of a particular trust must at the request of the trustee be
-- src:17357 | marked in the register in such a way as to identify them as being held
-- src:17358 | in respect of the trust.
@ref s 195(3) (src:17355-17358)
GIVEN `the shares are registered in a register of a company and held by a trustee in respect of a particular trust` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trustee has requested that the shares be marked in the register to identify them as held in respect of the trust` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 195(3) the shares must be marked in the register as held in respect of the trust` MEANS
    IF `the shares are registered in a register of a company and held by a trustee in respect of a particular trust` AND `the trustee has requested that the shares be marked in the register to identify them as held in respect of the trust`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Shares ... held by a trustee in respect of a particular trust must at the request of the trustee be marked in the register" (a duty gated by "at the request of"; the periods ruling items (b) and (c); the text names no bearer, so there is no regulative rule: forks F-W1, F-B1)

DECLARE `s 195(4) matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 195(4) a notice of a trust expressed, implied or constructive, not authorised by section 195`
    `s 195(4) the marking of shares under subsection (3)`
    `s 195(4) some other entry or notice`

-- src:17362 | (4) Subject to this section, no notice of any trust expressed, implied
-- src:17363 | or constructive may be entered in a register or be receivable by the
-- src:17364 | Registrar and no liabilities are affected by anything done pursuant to
-- src:17365 | subsection (1), (2) or (3) or pursuant to the law of any other place
-- src:17366 | which corresponds to this section and the company concerned is not
-- src:17367 | affected by notice of any trust by anything so done.
@ref s 195(4) (src:17362-17367)
GIVEN matter IS A `s 195(4) matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 195(4) the entry or receipt of the notice is barred` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `s 195(4) a notice of a trust expressed, implied or constructive, not authorised by section 195` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 195(4) the marking of shares under subsection (3)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to this section, no notice of any trust ... may be entered in a register" (the marking is authorised by subsection (3), the exception the text states; fork F-U1)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on "notice of any trust expressed, implied or constructive"

-- src:17362 | (4) Subject to this section, no notice of any trust expressed, implied
-- src:17363 | or constructive may be entered in a register or be receivable by the
-- src:17364 | Registrar and no liabilities are affected by anything done pursuant to
-- src:17365 | subsection (1), (2) or (3) or pursuant to the law of any other place
-- src:17366 | which corresponds to this section and the company concerned is not
-- src:17367 | affected by notice of any trust by anything so done.
@ref s 195(4) (src:17362-17367)
GIVEN `the thing was done pursuant to subsection (1), (2) or (3) or pursuant to the law of any other place which corresponds to this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 195(4) no liabilities are affected by what was done` MEANS
    IF `the thing was done pursuant to subsection (1), (2) or (3) or pursuant to the law of any other place which corresponds to this section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "no liabilities are affected by anything done pursuant to subsection (1), (2) or (3) or pursuant to the law of any other place which corresponds to this section"

-- src:17362 | (4) Subject to this section, no notice of any trust expressed, implied
-- src:17363 | or constructive may be entered in a register or be receivable by the
-- src:17364 | Registrar and no liabilities are affected by anything done pursuant to
-- src:17365 | subsection (1), (2) or (3) or pursuant to the law of any other place
-- src:17366 | which corresponds to this section and the company concerned is not
-- src:17367 | affected by notice of any trust by anything so done.
@ref s 195(4) (src:17362-17367)
GIVEN `the thing was done pursuant to subsection (1), (2) or (3) or pursuant to the law of any other place which corresponds to this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 195(4) the company is not affected by notice of any trust by anything so done` MEANS
    IF `the thing was done pursuant to subsection (1), (2) or (3) or pursuant to the law of any other place which corresponds to this section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the company concerned is not affected by notice of any trust by anything so done"

§ `Section 196: branch registers`

-- src:17373 | 196.—(1) A public company having a share capital may cause to be
-- src:17374 | kept in any place outside Singapore a branch register of members
-- src:17375 | which is deemed to be part of the company’s register of members.
@ref s 196(1) (src:17373-17375)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the place is outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
