@ref s 196(4) (src:17390-17393)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the period the standard of time allows, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that the standard of time in the section ("as soon as possible") allows for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 196 act`
`s 196(4) a public company must transmit a copy of every entry in its branch register` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 196(4) transmit to the office at which the principal register is kept a copy of every entry in the branch register`
    WITHIN `the period the standard of time allows, as found`   -- the section says "as soon as possible", its own standard of time, found as an input; Interpretation Act 1965 s 52 does not apply, because the section prescribes its own standard (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the public company did not transmit a copy of the entry in its branch register as soon as possible"

-- src:17398 | register, which is for all purposes of this Act deemed to be part of the
-- src:17399 | principal register.
