    MUST `s 196(4) cause to be kept at that office a duplicate of the branch register, duly entered up`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 196(4) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the public company did not cause a duplicate of its branch register to be kept" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: maintenance; see notes]

