    IF NOT `a corporation incorporated under the law of another country keeps in Singapore a branch register of its members by virtue of that law`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection is about a corporation that keeps in Singapore a branch register of its members by virtue of the law of another country
    ELSE (IF NOT `the Minister has by order declared that the provisions of this Act relating to inspection, place of keeping and rectification of registers of members apply to that branch register`
          THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the provisions apply "thereupon" on the Minister's order; without an order the text does not say they apply
          ELSE (IF `the order specifies a modification that bears on the provision in question`
                THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "subject to any modifications specified in the order"; the order is not among the sources
                ELSE JUST TRUE))

